[issue.1744]
number = 1744
title = "[Coherence] startup_refuses_a_chain_id_mismatch now starts its own node with a hard-coded chain id, while its spec task and decision 1896 still say it reads the gate environment's node"
revision = "a910fdedd579e63379ae6c2e4d4971990d28f8ad"
verdict = "spec-edit"
evidence = "Commit b014d764f685a682b73df7c3aaa1d4bc493b69f3 replaced the two environment reads with LocalNode::start, retained at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/host-tests/node_integration.rs:204, whose helper invokes the in-tree node at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/proof_native_reads.rs:613, and the test checks chain ID 125 through NodeRpc::connect at node_integration.rs:211 before asserting mismatch refusal at node_integration.rs:217; although services/agent/tools/run-real-node-tests.sh:36 still exports the manifest-derived chain ID, the done task 9.0.3 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:275533 retains the obsolete environment reads in do_6 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:275562 and the exclusive-node restriction in do_7 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:275563, so those steps must describe the disposable node and its checked chain ID 125, with an explicit exception for this test to decision 1896 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:4491 rather than changing the mismatch assertions."
close_comment = "The startup test uses a disposable in-tree node, checks its reported chain ID against 125, and verifies that a different configured chain ID refuses startup. Task 9.0.3's do_6 and do_7 and decision 1896's applicability to this test need a specification correction to describe that behavior instead of the obsolete environment-variable requirement."
